{
 "elemod": 2,
 "id": "digifilter",
 "version": "1.1a",
 "title": "Digi Filter",
 "description": "Adds per-track filter modes to the Digitakt mk1 on top of the stock LP/HP/EQ, using each track's own FREQ, RESO and filter envelope: BP (band pass), BP2 (a wider band pass), COMB and TRASH (two combs), and OB4/OB2 (the Oberheim OB-1's ladder, its 4-pole output and its 2-pole one: docs/ob1.md). Widens the Filter Type range to 13 and renames the new values, runs the extra DSP at the per-voice filter call (site 0x400780ba -> digifilter_dispatch), and overpaints the FLTR page's FREQ/RES response curve for the new modes from a core ev_draw handler (digifilter_draw: BP/BP2 a band-pass bell, COMB/TRASH comb teeth) when the page kind is 6. Stock TYPE values tail-call the stock filter and keep the stock curve. While COMB/TRASH is selected the RESO/GAIN knob is the comb feedback (0..127) and the second FLTR page's free C/G encoders add Harmonics/Damping controls (labelled HARM/DAMP), alongside the stock Base/Width/Env Delay/SRR knobs which keep working. See README.md.",
 "category": "Sound",
 "author": "Digital Alchemy DSP",
 "license": "GPL-2.0-or-later",
 "target": {
  "device": "digitakt-mk1",
  "product": "Digitakt mk1",
  "os": "1.54",
  "syx_sha256": "f78ba80fa7b1da5fb0e1ff61ad61e9e71aafe79f4364fc49679f3651353e3cf6",
  "section3_sha256": "5c58bf9e3949ef09977c5fc007a61e8d026931f67f1621238379dfb8ee4d31a2",
  "section3_len": 2479680
 },
